  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Monitoring and Reducing Expansion of the Agricultural Frontier in the Chiquibul- Maya Mountains</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Project will reduce forest loss in Belizes Chiquibul-Maya Mountains by increasing law enforcement efforts and community forest management. The project is intended to conserve Chiquibul National Park, Vaca Forest Reserve and Columbia River Forest Reserve by addressing the impacts of agricultural encroachment and illegal natural resource extraction. Specific activities include: 1) air and ground monitoring and patrolling in urgent hotspots for illegal forest clearing for agriculture, poaching and gold panning; 2) training rangers on how to operate in the forest, law enforcement monitoring training, and search and arrest procedures; 3) instituting a community to community exchange program between the Vaca Forest Reserve and the Guatemala Maya Biosphere on community forest concession management; 4) supporting Friends of the Vaca community group to test and implement a pilot sustainable forest product project; and 5) strengthening bi-national coordination and inter-agency cooperation to more effectively address this trans-boundary environmental threat.</narrative>
  </description>
